 "desc": "Time to exploit a MIPS stack overflow! The function has a 16-byte buffer and saves $ra above it on the stack. Overflow the buffer to overwrite the saved $ra with the address of win(). When the function epilogue executes lw $ra, 20($sp) followed by jr $ra, it will jump to your chosen address. Note: MIPS is big-endian, so addresses are written MSB first (opposite of x86 little-endian).",
 "source": [
  "#include <stdio.h>",
  "",
  "/* MIPS big-endian — addresses stored MSB first */",
  "",
  "void win() {",
  "    printf(\"FLAG{mips_ra_hijack}\\n\");",
  "}",
  "",
  "void vuln() {",
  "    char buf[16];",
  "    /* Prologue saved $ra at 20($sp) */",
  "    gets(buf);",
  "    /* Epilogue: lw $ra, 20($sp); jr $ra */",
  "}",
  "",
  "int main() {",
  "    vuln();",
  "    return 0;",
  "}"
